Suggests: jackd2 | pipewire-jack
Description: low-latency scsynth-compatible audio synthesis server
 SuperSonic is a scsynth-compatible synth powered by clockwork, a substrate
 providing audio device I/O, MIDI, OSC, game controller input, the transport
 clock and Ableton Link. Its synthesis code was forked from SuperCollider's
 scsynth. The server accepts scsynth's command-line flags and OSC commands,
 so clients that start and drive scsynth, such as Sonic Pi, can start and
 drive it the same way.
 .
 Ableton Link session sync (including Link Audio streaming), MIDI I/O,
 game controller input, and OSC cue networking are built in. Commands
 arrive as OSC over UDP by default; TCP, Unix-socket, and shared-memory
 command transports are also available.
